# state: any   (classifier-path benchmark opening, fixed for Controller
# Select -- #433 lane.topspinroute1018, from dispatch/results/
# z-1792314505-lanelocal-3439642, 10-18 02:08)
#
# Top Spin (4D530035). `drive generic` correctly presses A through Main
# Menu, Settings, Venue and Court (that run's route-state.tsv: "ingame_menu"
# presses 1-4, all of them right), then gets stuck on Controller Select the
# same way -- pathclass names it the same `ingame_menu`/`submenu` as the
# four screens before it, and A alone does nothing there: both pads sit in
# the middle with no team assigned. 25 presses later: ROUTE FAIL "stuck on
# ingame_menu after 25 presses". The recorded first-run route
# (fps786-topspin.route, step 16) clears it with `axis HATX min` then
# `axis HATX mid`, then A.
#
# So this route splits in two: `drive` for boot/intro/logo/title and the
# four menu screens the classifier already gets right -- its whole point is
# not needing to know how long an intro video plays, which varied by two
# skip cycles and ~29 s in the one run on record -- then fps786's own
# steps 14-25, copied verbatim (same waits, same presses, including its own
# wasted A and START on Controller Select before the hat move that actually
# works), since that stretch does not depend on first-run vs kept-profile.
#
# 75 s for the `drive` step: the tsv shows Controller Select first reached
# at t=52.5 and the 25th press (FAIL) at t=123.4 -- a 70.9 s gap fixed by
# the profile's menu_gap_s, not by anything that varies run to run. 75 s
# clears 52.5 with margin and sits under a worst-case FAIL floor estimated
# at ~85-87 s. See docs/lanes/topspinroute1018/NOTES.md for the full
# reasoning and the residual risk (an unusually fast run could still rack up
# 25 stuck presses before 75 s) -- not device-proven; the run after this
# lane checks it for real.
drive generic 75
# Whatever screen that left us on (Controller Select, or Court/Venue/
# Settings if the bound undershot), fps786-topspin.route steps 14-16,
# unchanged: a press A and a press START that only do something if we are
# not already on Controller Select, then the hat move that clears it.
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 17.0
shot s15-submenu
# step 15 [submenu] Controller Select screen unchanged after A (or Venue/Court, advanced by it)
press START 120
wait 0.6
wait 10.3
shot s16-submenu
# step 16 [submenu] Controller Select screen: 1P still in the middle with no team, A/START do nothing
axis HATX min
axis HATX mid
wait 0.6
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 12.5
shot s17-submenu
# step 17 [submenu] Player Select: 1P and COM both show P. Sampras, avatar highlighted bottom-left
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 8.7
shot s18-submenu
# step 18 [submenu] Exhibition Player Select: 1P shows P. Sampras with READY banner, COM with stats
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 11.8
shot s19-submenu
# step 19 [submenu] Head-to-Head exhibition screen, both players READY; prompt shows 'A Play match'
press A 120
wait 0.6
wait 17.7
shot s20-loading
# step 20 [loading] Match intro: 'The Oceania Tennis Championship' stadium and court, LOADING
wait 13.8
shot s21-loading
wait 13.4
shot s22-loading
wait 11.5
shot s23-loading
# step 23 [loading] Match intro loading, EXHIBITION/PRESS START banner
press START 120
wait 0.6
wait 13.3
shot s24-loading
# step 24 [loading] Melbourne stadium, player walking out with racket bag
press START 120
wait 0.6
wait 17.0
shot s25-gameplay
# step 25 [gameplay] Match has loaded; player at baseline ready to serve
wait 3
mark gameplay
# genre loop: tennis, move to the ball and swing -- never START (unchanged
# from the previous gen-top-spin.route)
repeat forever {
    axis LX max
    wait 0.8
    axis LX min
    wait 0.8
    axis LX mid
    press A 300
    wait 1.5
    press X 300
    wait 1.5
}
